.\" mshellctl(1) — margo desktop-shell IPC client
.\" Command list mirrors `mshellctl --help`; per-command detail is in
.\" `mshellctl <CMD> --help`.
.TH MSHELLCTL 1 "2026-11-05" "margo" "Margo Manual"
.SH NAME
mshellctl \- control the margo desktop shell (mshell)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mshellctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ SUBCOMMAND "] [" ARGS .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mshellctl
drives the running margo desktop shell
.RB ( mshell )
over the session D-Bus (service
.IR com.mshell.Shell ).
It controls the
.IR shell "\(em"
menus, bars, audio, the session, notifications, and the companion tools.
.PP
This is distinct from
.BR mctl (1),
which controls the
.I compositor
(windows, tags, layouts). The two talk to different daemons \(em don't
conflate them.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Surfaces"
.TP
.B menu \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Open, close or toggle a shell menu:
.IR control-center ", " dashboard ", " mdash ", " clipboard ", " cpu-dashboard ", " audio-dashboard ,
.IR ssh-sessions ", " session ", " plugin ", \[char46]\&.\&.\&."
.TP
.B bar \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Show, hide or toggle the bars:
.IR top " | " bottom " | " toggle-all " | " reveal-all " | " hide-all .
.TP
.B hidden-bar \fIACTION\fR [\fINAME\fR]
Control the Hidden Bar drawer widget
.RI ( toggle " | " expand " | " collapse " | " pin " | " unpin );
with no
.I NAME
every drawer is affected.
.TP
.B custom-refresh \fR[\fINAME\fR]
Re-run a custom bar pill's
.B exec
now instead of waiting for its interval; with no
.I NAME
every custom pill refreshes.
.TP
.B dock \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The standalone mdock surface:
.IR toggle " | " show " | " hide " | " "activate \fIN\fR" .
.TP
.B settings \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Open or close the Settings window
.RI ( open " | " close ).
.TP
.B wizard
Open the in-shell setup wizard (a layer-shell menu).
.TP
.B inspect
Open the GTK4 inspector (find CSS node ids and classes).
.SS "Audio and media"
.TP
.B audio \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Volume, mute, mic and device switching \(em e.g.
.IR volume-up ", " "volume " PERCENT ", " mute ", " "output " next ", " mic-mute .
.TP
.B media \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Control MPRIS players and native MPD:
.IR toggle ", " next ", " prev ", " status ", " list .
.TP
.B brightness \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Backlight control:
.IR up " | " down .
.TP
.B mtune \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Control the
.B mtune
music player directly (no shell needed): playback, seek, volume, rate,
repeat, shuffle, queue, library and playlists, status and metadata.
.SS "Appearance"
.TP
.B wallpaper \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Cycle the wallpaper:
.IR next " | " prev " | " random .
.TP
.B set-wallpaper \fIPATH\fR
Set the current wallpaper to a specific image.
.TP
.B theme \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect or switch the colour scheme (the same picker as Settings \(->
Theme \(-> Color Scheme), applied live with no restart:
.IR list " [" \-\-names\-only "] | " get " | " "set \fINAME\fR" .
.B set
matching ignores case and
.RB ` \- '/` _ '/space
separators, so
.IR kenp ", " tokyo\-night " and " "\(dqTokyo Night\(dq"
all resolve;
.B theme list
prints the valid names.
.B theme bundle list
prints the saved theme bundles (Settings \(-> Theme \(-> Bundles) as
tab-separated name, scheme and wallpaper count, marking the active one;
.B theme bundle apply \fINAME\fR
applies one (scheme, matugen settings and wallpaper) in one step. While a
bundle is active,
.B wallpaper next\fR|\fBprevious\fR|\fBrandom
step through its wallpapers only.
.SS "Session and notifications"
.TP
.B session \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Session and power actions:
.IR menu " | " lock " | " logout " | " suspend " | " reboot " | " shutdown .
.B session boot\-entries
lists the UEFI boot entries (efibootmgr);
.B session reboot\-into \fIENTRY\fR
sets the one-shot BootNext to
.I ENTRY
(its number, e.g.
.IR 0003 ,
or its exact label) through a polkit prompt, then reboots.
.TP
.B lock \fR[\fBactivate\fR | \fBcheck\fR]
Lock the session. Bare
.B lock
locks;
.B lock check
prints
.I locked
or
.IR unlocked .
.TP
.B notification \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The notification centre:
.IR open " | " clear " | " read " | " "dnd \fR[\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR]" " | " count .
.TP
.B toast \fR[\fB\-\-icon\fR \fIICON\fR] [\fB\-\-severity\fR \fILEVEL\fR] \fITITLE\fR [\fIBODY\fR]
Show a transient toast \(em the
.BR notify-send (1)
equivalent for the toast surface (no notification history).
.TP
.B gamemode \fR[\fIon\fR | \fIoff\fR | \fItoggle\fR | \fIstatus\fR]
Game Mode: drop compositor effects, silence notifications and keep the
session awake; optionally (Settings \(-> Game Mode) switch the power profile,
hide the bars and the dock, hold back the OSD, stop drawing the wallpaper,
pause media, clear notification pop-ups and run an enter / exit command.
Turning it off puts back what turning it on changed (default:
.IR toggle ).
.SS "Focus and breaks"
.TP
.B pomodoro \fR[\fItoggle\fR | \fIstart\fR | \fIpause\fR | \fIskip\fR | \fIreset\fR | \fIreset\-all\fR | \fIstatus\fR]
The Pomodoro timer (work, short break, long break). Prints one status line
after the action, e.g.
.IR "phase=work state=running remaining=24:13 session=1/4 completed=0"
(default:
.IR status ).
Lengths and auto-start live in Settings \(-> Widgets \(-> Alarm Clock.
.TP
.B eyecare \fR[\fIbreak\fR | \fIskip\fR | \fIreset\fR | \fIon\fR | \fIoff\fR | \fItoggle\fR | \fIstatus\fR]
The 20-20-20 eye-care reminder: every 20 minutes of screen time, look about
6 m (20 ft) away for 20 seconds. Only time at the keyboard counts; stepping
away resets the count. Off by default
.RI ( on
enables it). Prints one status line after the action, e.g.
.I state=active next\-break\-in=840s
(default:
.IR status ).
.SS "Capture"
.TP
.B screenshot \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Capture to file and clipboard:
.IR region ", " window ", " output ", " full ", " repeat ", " ocr ", " qr ", " palette ", " measure .
.B \-\-pin
floats a capture on screen (always on top);
.B ocr \-\-translate
copies the translation;
.B measure
copies a region's size.
.TP
.B screenrecord \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The shell's screen recorder:
.IR start " | " stop " | " toggle .
.TP
.B clipboard \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Clipboard history:
.IR list ", " "copy \fIID\fR" ", " "pin \fIID\fR" ", " "delete \fIID\fR" ", " clear ", " wipe .
.TP
.B translate \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Headless translation: translate the selection
.RI ( selection ),
the clipboard
.RI ( clipboard )
or a string
.RI ( "text \fITEXT\fR" ),
copy the result and toast it.
.TP
.B qr \fR[\fITEXT\fR | \fB\-\-clipboard\fR | \fB\-\-wifi\fR | \fB\-\-hotspot\fR]
Show a QR code to scan from a phone in the QR menu: a text or URL
.RI ( \- " reads standard input),"
the clipboard's text, the Wi\-Fi network this machine is on, or its hotspot.
The Wi\-Fi codes contain the network password; the shell reads it from
NetworkManager itself and hands it to
.BR qrencode (1)
on standard input, never on a command line.
.SS "Companion tools"
.TP
.B calendar \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Events and accounts via
.BR mcal :
.IR today ", " "agenda \fR[\fIDAYS\fR]" ", " "on \fIDATE\fR" ", " "account \fR\&.\|.\|." .
.TP
.B vpn \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Mullvad VPN via
.BR mvpn :
.IR status ", " connect ", " disconnect ", " toggle ", " reconnect ", " random ", " fastest ", " menu .
.TP
.B power \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Power profile via
.BR mpower :
.IR status ", " cycle ", " "set \fIPROFILE\fR" ", " pause ", " resume .
.TP
.B layout \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Saved layouts via
.BR mlayout :
.IR list ", " current ", " "set \fINAME\fR" ", " next ", " prev ", " preview ", " pick .
.TP
.B osk \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The on-screen keyboard
.RB ( mkeys ):
.IR show " | " hide " | " toggle .
.TP
.B color \fR[\fB\-\-copy\fR] [\fB\-\-notify\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] \&.\|.\|.
Pick a screen colour with
.BR mpicker
and print it
.RI ( hex ", " rgb ", " hsl ", " cmyk ).
.TP
.B play \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The mpv companion: start, toggle, play or queue a URL / path / the
clipboard (YouTube videos resume where you stopped; history and positions
in
.IR ~/.local/state/margo/youtube/ ;
.B play forget
drops them), download with yt-dlp, window control, and the native
video-wallpaper engine
.RB ( "play wallpaper" ).
.SS "System and diagnostics"
.TP
.B bluetooth \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
The auto-connect engine:
.IR toggle ", " connect ", " disconnect ", " "connect-number \fIN\fR" .
.TP
.B log \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Shell file logging
.RI ( ~/.local/state/margo/logs/mshell-*.log ):
.IR "level \fILEVEL\fR" ", " enable ", " disable ", " path ", " open .
.TP
.B plugin \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage installed WASM plugins:
.IR list ", " "reload \fINAME\fR" ", " "keybind \fR\&.\|.\|." .
.TP
.B doctor
One-shot health check of the shell: session-bus reachability, whether
.B com.mshell.Shell
is up, and whether the running shell matches this
.BR mshellctl 's
version (a stale shell after an upgrade is the usual "my new feature is
missing" cause). Exits non-zero on error. Run
.B mctl doctor
for the compositor side.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Emit a shell-completion script to stdout
.RI ( bash " | " zsh " | " fish " | " elvish " | " powershell ).
.TP
.B quit
Quit the shell (the compositor keeps running).
.PP
Run
.B mshellctl
.I COMMAND
.B \-\-help
for the full subcommand and argument surface.
.SH EXAMPLES
.in +4n
.EX
mshellctl menu control-center     # toggle the quick-settings panel
mshellctl menu mdash              # toggle the dashboard
mshellctl audio volume 60         # set output volume to 60%
mshellctl audio mute
mshellctl brightness up
mshellctl media toggle            # play/pause the active player
mshellctl wallpaper next
mshellctl theme set kenp          # switch colour scheme live
mshellctl theme list              # show every scheme name
mshellctl doctor                  # shell health check
mshellctl completions zsh         # emit zsh completion script
mshellctl lock
mshellctl qr \-\-wifi              # let a phone join this Wi\-Fi
.EE
.in
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR margo (1),
.BR mctl (1),
.BR mdots (1)
